# __APP_TITLE__

A generated local-web platform app hosted at `__APP_ROUTE__`.

## Development

```sh
npm install
npm run dev
```

The app runs independently with the shared UI package's fallback theme. Set `VITE_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=__APP_ROUTE__/` to exercise its hosted path prefix.

The shared header includes Context export. The generated adapter in `src/contextExport.ts` exports only this app's private foundation state; enrich it with reviewed domain context as features are added.

Interactive HTML export is optional and separate from Context export. When the
app needs it, add one shared app-owned contract/decoder, a coherent
`buildSnapshot()` returning distinct `snapshotData` and `viewState`, an offline
entry that imports the same contract, and `localWebInteractiveExport()` in the
Vite configuration. Static compiled content may use empty snapshot data, and an
app without restorable presentation state may use empty view state. Service apps
must validate the captured backend response and explicitly adapt backend-only
actions for offline use. Follow the framework README's compatibility, CSP,
sensitivity, size, and browser-verification contract; do not copy a private
app's payload shape into this template.

__SERVICE_DEVELOPMENT__

## Verification

Resolve `LOCAL_WEB` exactly as `AGENTS.md` and the installed
`$local-web-app-development` skill prescribe, then run:

```sh
"$LOCAL_WEB" app doctor --repository .
npm run check
npm run test:e2e
```

`npm run check` is entirely app-local: it runs lint, unit tests, and the production build. `"$LOCAL_WEB" app check --repository .` runs the structural doctor first, then orchestrates the app-local checks and browser tests.
